    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "content": "Media Queries"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "A media query in CSS lets you apply styles based on conditions like screen size, orientation (portrait or landscape), or resolution."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Here's what the basic syntax looks like:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "css",
      "content": "@media (condition) {\n    /* CSS rules here */\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Here, you use the @media keyword to define a media query. The CSS rules specified in the query are applied when the condition is satisfied."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "html",
      "content": "1<body></body>"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "css",
      "content": "1body {\n2    background-color: lightgreen;\n3}\n4\n5/* Media query for screens with width \n6above or equal to 600px */\n7@media (min-width: 600px) {\n8    body {\n9        background-color: lightblue;\n10    }\n11}"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Here's how the browser output looks in different screen sizes:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "1. Default Style (When the Screen Has a Width Below 600px)"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "alt": "Style for Smaller Screen",
      "src": "data:image/png;base64,"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "2. Style When the Screen Has a Width Equal to or Over 600px"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "alt": "Style for Larger Screen",
      "src": "data:image/png;base64,"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "In our code, the media query uses the condition min-width: 600px. This means the specified styles will only be applied when the device's width is more than or equal to 600px."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "So, by default, the background color is lightgreen. However, for devices with widths greater than 600px, the background color will be lightblue."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "content": "How does it work?"
    },
